  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting gender equality in conflict affected Lebanon by responding to GBV needs for women, youth and LGBTQI+</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA aims at supporting advancement of gender equality in Lebanon by supporting the implementation of the national strategy for women in Lebanon (2022-2030), in particular by supporting  social service standards  and service delivery in 3 Social Development Centres (SDC) as well as the monitoring of the strategy. The SDCs will be supported with a combination Gender Based Violence and adolescent youth friendly information and services on Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights. Moreover a clinic in Beirut will serve LGBTQI+ population with sexual health services. In terms of coordination, the project will support PSEA/AAP Coordinator and LGBTQI+ taskforce coordinator.</narrative>
  </description>
